      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(proxy-capture): widen local peer detection to full 127.0.0.0/8 range",
        "body": "## What\n\nChanged local peer host detection in the proxy-capture dashboard from `host.startsWith(\"127.0.0.1:\")` to `host.startsWith(\"127.\")`, covering the full 127.0.0.0/8 loopback range.\n\n## Why\n\nThe proxy-capture dashboard classifies hosts into `localPeers` for display grouping. Model endpoints bound to other loopback addresses (e.g., `127.0.0.2:11434`) were not counted as local peers. This is a data-quality fix — not a security boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Affected file: `src/proxy-capture/store.sqlite.ts`\n- The canonical `isLoopbackIpAddress` in `packages/net-policy/src/ip.ts` covers the full 127/8 range\n- The `host.startsWith(\"127.\")` pattern is already used correctly in `src/gateway/model-pricing-cache.ts`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
